dsh-workplan README · Use it：- five headline numbers: **tasks / work items / done / in progress / blocked**;
   - plan cards grouped into **In progress**, **Ended** and **Completed**, each with a completion rate. **Ended** means the turn has stopped (nothing is running) while the plan is still unfinished; the card also says where it stopped (budget spent / stuck / not started) and resuming is one sentence away;
   - expand any plan to see per-stage progress and who owns each work item.

dsh-workplan README · Three phases and self-learning (2.0.2)：Phase 3 also requires a **retrospective** (`retrospective` inside `phases.verification`):

1. `problems` — every problem met in the process (symptom + root cause);
2. `detours` — wrong turns, rework, dead ends (empty array when genuinely none; do not invent);
3. `resolutions` — how those problems were finally solved;
4. `prevention` — executable "when X, first do Y" rules that stop the same mistake from happening again.
